#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:1
msgid "Where each logic lives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:3
msgid ""
"A format's reading is split across three segments, and the split is not a"
" matter of taste. Putting a piece of reasoning in the wrong one is the "
"easiest mistake to make in this whole area, and the one that costs most "
"later, because the misplacement is invisible until a second document "
"arrives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md
msgid "Segment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md
msgid "What belongs to it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md
msgid "What it is handed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md
msgid "`pdf_extract`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md
msgid ""
"**layout and geometry**: which lines, which column, which band, which "
"cell continues which"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md
msgid "the page's lines, and nothing else"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md
msgid "`text_filter`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md
msgid ""
"**all the interpretation of the text**: what a word means, which entity a"
" name is, what to keep"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md
msgid "the blocks the first segment made"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md
msgid "`deserialize`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md
msgid "**only the casts**: a string to a number, a string to a date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md
msgid "the blocks the second segment kept"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:13
msgid "The rule, in one sentence each"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:15
msgid ""
"**`pdf_extract` may not know what anything means.** It does not know "
"which companies are of interest, which sub-funds the job has seen, or "
"what a word says. It knows where things are."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:18
msgid ""
"**`text_filter` may not look at the page.** It never sees a line, a "
"coordinate or a font: it sees blocks. Everything that is *where* has "
"already been decided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:21
msgid ""
"**`deserialize` may not decide anything.** `1.234` to `1234`, "
"`15/03/2029` to a date. If a conversion needs to know which convention "
"the page uses, the convention is a **parameter** of the cast and not a "
"branch in it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:25
msgid "Why it is drawn there"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:27
msgid ""
"Because the two halves vary independently. A report that changes its "
"typesetting between two years changes its geometry and not its "
"vocabulary; a report translated into another language changes its "
"vocabulary and not its geometry. Code that mixes them has to be rewritten"
" for either."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:31
msgid ""
"The clearest evidence is a datum written in several ways by one issuer. "
"When a report states its sub-fund renamings as prose in one document and "
"as a dated list in another, the **text_filter** changes and the "
"`pdf_extract` does not: both documents hand over the same section of the "
"same page, and what differs is what the sentences say. Had the reading of"
" the sentence been written into the extraction, there would now be two "
"extractions of one section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:37
msgid "Three decisions, and where each one went"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:39
msgid ""
"These are measured cases, and each of them could plausibly have gone into"
" a different segment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:41
msgid ""
"**A name that wrapped.** A table cell too long for its column arrives as "
"two lines with their own coordinates. Putting them back together is "
"*layout*: it happens in `pdf_extract`, and the pieces are joined with "
"**nothing** between them, because a generator breaking at a word boundary"
" leaves the space at the end of the first piece and breaking inside a "
"word leaves none — the page already says how they meet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:47
msgid ""
"**A table row whose first column is empty.** Note 16 of one report lists "
"two delegates for one sub-fund, the second on a row of its own with the "
"fund column blank — a cell spanning two rows. Repeating the fund on that "
"row is reading the **layout**, so it is `pdf_extract`. Without it the "
"second delegate vanishes silently, which is the failure this whole "
"division is meant to make visible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:53
msgid ""
"**A liability printed in brackets.** `(21,301)` is not a negative number:"
" it is a typographic convention for a deduction, and the output schema "
"wants the magnitude because it checks that liabilities plus net assets "
"make the total. Reading it is therefore neither geometry nor meaning but "
"a **convention of the cast** — `Amount cast: int + magnitude` — and the "
"brackets come off before the conversion, which is the only way the "
"conversion can happen at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:59
msgid "The one that is always tempting, and always wrong"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:61
msgid ""
"Where a datum is hard to isolate, it is tempting to extract generously "
"and let the `text_filter` throw away the excess — it is going to filter "
"against the funds of interest anyway, so the noise will not reach the "
"output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/where-each-logic-lives.md:65
msgid ""
"It will not reach the output *of this run*. It will reach the output of a"
" run with a different target list, which is the run the next person "
"makes. The filter is a safety net, not an anchor: find an honest anchor "
"first, and let the filter stand behind it."
msgstr ""

